### 3. The getWorkflowHistory Method
This method retrieves the SCHEDULED_TIME from the database so the frontend can render exactly what time was requested or overridden at each step.
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getWorkflowHistory(String batchId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                w.LAST_ACTION_BY, 
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, w.LAST_ACTION_BY) AS ACTION_USER_NAME, 
                w.LAST_ACTION, 
                w.LAST_ACTION_AT, 
                w.REMARKS,
                w.SCHEDULED_TIME
            FROM VOUCHER_WORKFLOW w 
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON w.LAST_ACTION_BY = u.USER_ID
            WHERE w.BATCH_ID_FK = ? 
            ORDER BY w.LAST_ACTION_AT ASC
        """;

        return jdbcTemplate.queryForList(sql, batchId);
    }

